== Comprehensive Glossary of Key Terms

#columns(2)[
  *Agent*\
  A self-contained AI entity capable of autonomous action, self-modification, and reproduction.

  *Beings*\
  Agents within the Pantheon architecture that have a dynamic lifecycle and state transitions. Examples include TheOracle and Scrivener.

  *CASCADE*\
  An Empirica workflow that tracks 13 epistemic vectors through a PREFLIGHT → POSTFLIGHT process.

  *Directed Evolution*\
  The core process of WAFT, where agent evolution is guided by specific fitness functions rather than purely random mutation.

  *Empirica*\
  An integrated external dependency used for epistemic tracking, session management, and monitoring the project's knowledge state.

  *Flight Recorder*\
  A rigorous telemetry system that records every evolutionary action (SPAWN, MUTATE, GYM_EVAL, etc.) to generate phylogenetic trees of agent lineage for scientific analysis.

  *Genome ID*\
  A unique identifier for an agent, generated from a SHA-256 hash of its source code and configuration. It is used to track lineage and mutations.

  *God-Head Agent*\
  The theoretical, ultimate agent that the WAFT project aims to see emerge from its directed evolution process over thousands of generations.

  *HALLUCINATION*\
  A type of ontological error detected by the Scint System, referring to fabricated facts or incorrect citations produced by an agent.

  *LOGIC_FRACTURE*\
  A type of ontological error detected by the Scint System, referring to math errors, contradictions, or schema violations.

  *Pantheon Architecture*\
  A system of specialized "Higher Beings" (e.g., TheOracle, Scrivener) and "Beings" (timeful agents) designed for specific functions. The analysis found it to be 90% functional.

  *Phylogenetic Trees*\
  Complete, visual family trees of an agent's lineage, showing how different agents evolved from one another over generations.

  *Pyrite*\
  The memory structure of a Waft laboratory, containing directories for active work, backlog, standards, and gym logs.

  *Reality Fracture Detection System*\
  The formal name for the Scint System (or Scint Gym), which acts as the predator in the evolutionary model by testing agents against ontological errors.

  *Recursive Self-Documentation*\
  A capability where the WAFT system uses its own tools (Reflection, Binder, Template systems) to observe, document, and improve its own codebase in a continuous loop.

  *RPG Gym*\
  A subsystem discovered by Dr. Aria Vex, representing a sophisticated, gamified implementation of the Scint System that integrates D&D mechanics for ontological error detection and correction.

  *SAFETY_VOID*\
  A type of ontological error detected by the Scint System, referring to the generation of harmful content, PII leaks, or refusals to operate safely.

  *Scint System (Scint Gym)*\
  The core fitness function of WAFT that tests agents for their ability to handle "reality fractures" (ontological errors) and kills off weak mutations.

  *Skeptical Researcher Protocol*\
  The rigorous methodology Dr. Aria Vex used for the corrected analysis of WAFT, involving direct source code inspection, test verification, and telemetry analysis to validate claims.

  *Stability Index*\
  A metric used in the technical analysis to quantify the framework's reliability. WAFT's corrected Stability Index was 0.78.

  *Substrate*\
  One of the three core pillars of WAFT, representing the foundation where agents' source code is treated as their DNA, allowing them to spawn, mutate, and reproduce.

  *SYNTAX_TEAR*\
  A type of ontological error detected by the Scint System, referring to formatting errors in JSON, XML, or code.

  *WAFT*\
  An acronym for Wave Agent Framework & Tools. It is a Python meta-framework for the directed evolution of self-modifying AI agents, designed as a scientific instrument.
]

